Chapter: EdgeMeshMint

  cites Engine chapter EdgeMesh
  cites Mesh chapter EdgeMeshRewards
  cites CodexMagic chapter ChainCore
  cites CodexMagic chapter TransactionValidator

 `EdgeMeshGameServers.md` phase 4, stage 4: economic anti-abuse. Phase 3 stage 3
 credits a per-plane wallet for any amount a caller hands over, so the mesh's own
 book is the only thing standing between a wrong reward and a balance.

 THE TRANSACTION IS VALIDATED BEFORE THE LEDGER IS TOUCHED. A guard that credits
 and then rolls back on a refusal answers the same words as this one, and the
 ledger left behind after a refusal is the whole point of the guard.

 The chain transaction is the AUTHORITY and the ledger is the mesh's own book:
 the transaction names an account and an amount the platform key is permitted to
 award, and the ledger names the plane the coins land on.

Section: A Reward As A Transaction

  mesh-reward-tx : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> ChainTx
  mesh-reward-tx (platform-key) (receiver) (coins) (nonce) (timestamp) (private-key) =
    sign-transaction platform-key receiver coins TxReward nonce timestamp private-key

Section: Settling Behind The Guard

  MintOutcome =
    | Minted (Ledger) (Integer)
    | MintRefused (Ledger) (Text)

  guarded-settle : ChainState, Integer, Ledger, Integer, Text, Text, MatchReward, ChainTx -> MintOutcome
  guarded-settle (chain) (platform-key) (l) (match-id) (winner-plane) (loser-plane) (rw) (tx) =
    let v = validate-tx chain tx platform-key
    in if (v.valid) == False then MintRefused (l) (v.reason)
    else mint-after-guard (settle l match-id winner-plane loser-plane rw) l

  mint-after-guard : SettleResult, Ledger -> MintOutcome
  mint-after-guard (r) (before) =
    when r.sr-outcome
      is Settled (plane) (coins) -> Minted (r.sr-ledger) (coins)
      is SettleRefused (why) -> MintRefused (before) (why)

Section: Reporting

  mint-ledger : MintOutcome -> Ledger
  mint-ledger (o) =
    when o
      is Minted (l) (coins) -> l
      is MintRefused (l) (why) -> l

  mint-label : MintOutcome -> Text
  mint-label (o) =
    when o
      is Minted (l) (coins) -> "minted " & show coins
      is MintRefused (l) (why) -> "refused: " & why
